      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I thought the SDK documentation has an explanation. The quest hardware can only do so much, so the SDK actually blocked audio for a long time, and people were using really old or edited SDK to get sounds on Quest avatars. \n\nI never got an answer about that when Quest still had some audio on avatars, nobody was talking how they did it. \n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/audio-for-quest-avatars\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-30/p/allow-audiosource-on-android-quest\n\nOn this one someone is claiming that the quest can't handle 40 users talking, good thing the instance limit is 80...\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/bring-back-avatar-audio-for-the-quest\n\nPerson requesting avatar sounds is saying they feel embarrassed making thier own sound effects.\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/allow-audio-source-on-quest-avatar\n\nMarch 7 2021, the phrasing here makes it clear that some avatars have audio while the SDK blocks adding them.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
